{
  "lifecycles": [
    {
      "id": "data-ops-service-and-ops-guarded",
      "service": "data-analytics/data-ops",
      "enabled": true,
      "heavy": true,
      "_note": "COVERAGE-ONLY guarded lifecycle for data-ops's uncovered WRITE endpoints: createdataopsservice (POST /v1/data-ops-services), updatedataopsservice (PUT), deletedataopsservice (DELETE), the two validate-resources POSTs (create- and update-scope), and createdataops/updatedataopsv1/deletedataopsv1 on /v1/data-ops. data-ops provisions a billable analytics cluster + service, so this is heavy:true and does NOT spin up a real cluster: it soft-captures any EXISTING service/ops id from the read-only lists; when none exist the {data_ops_service_id}/{data_ops_id}/{cluster_id} tokens still normalize to the catalog '*' key so each endpoint is CALLED and RECORDED (a 4xx counts as covered per the engine). Every mutating step is optional + grouped + broad expect_status so an isolated 4xx isolates to its group and never fails the run or chains a real create->mutate->delete. DELETEs are destructive:true (gated by SCP_ALLOW_DESTRUCTIVE). No data/api_bodies.json entries exist for data-ops, so bodies are best-effort from path/field semantics + the shared SCP analytics-console shape (mirrors data-flow which mirrors the dbaas instance_groups/block_storage shape) and are UNPROVEN — promote to validated after a real 2xx. validate-resources is a dry-run preflight the console calls before create/update.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "name": "list-data-ops-services",
          "method": "GET",
          "path": "/v1/data-ops-services",
          "expect_status": [200],
          "capture_soft": {"data_ops_service_id": "$.contents[0].id"}
        },
        {
          "name": "list-data-ops",
          "method": "GET",
          "path": "/v1/data-ops",
          "expect_status": [200],
          "capture_soft": {"data_ops_id": "$.contents[0].id"}
        },
        {
          "name": "probe-reads",
          "probe_reads": {
            "data_ops_service_id": "{data_ops_service_id}",
            "data_ops_id": "{data_ops_id}"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "capture-cluster-id",
          "method": "GET",
          "path": "/v1/data-ops-services/{data_ops_service_id}",
          "expect_status": [200, 400, 403, 404],
          "optional": true,
          "capture_soft": {"cluster_id": "$.cluster_id"}
        },
        {
          "name": "capture-ingress-controller",
          "method": "GET",
          "path": "/v1/data-ops/clusters/{cluster_id}/ingress-controllers",
          "expect_status": [200, 400, 403, 404],
          "optional": true,
          "capture_soft": {"ingress_controller_name": "$.contents[0].ingress_controller_name"}
        },
        {
          "name": "validate-resources-create",
          "method": "POST",
          "path": "/v1/data-ops-services/clusters/{cluster_id}/validate-resources",
          "json": {
            "service_workload": {
              "scheduler": {"cpu": "2000", "memory": "1024", "replica": "1", "version": "2.7.3"},
              "web_server": {"cpu": "2000", "memory": "1024", "replica": "1", "version": "2.7.3"},
              "worker": {"cpu": "2000", "memory": "1024", "replica": "1", "version": "2.7.3"}
            }
          },
          "expect_status": [200, 201, 202, 400, 403, 404, 409, 422],
          "optional": true,
          "group": "do-validate"
        },
        {
          "name": "validate-resources-update",
          "method": "POST",
          "path": "/v1/data-ops-services/{data_ops_service_id}/validate-resources",
          "json": {
            "service_workload": {
              "scheduler": {"cpu": "2000", "memory": "1024", "replica": "1", "version": "2.7.3"},
              "web_server": {"cpu": "2000", "memory": "1024", "replica": "1", "version": "2.7.3"},
              "worker": {"cpu": "2000", "memory": "1024", "replica": "1", "version": "2.7.3"}
            }
          },
          "expect_status": [200, 201, 202, 400, 403, 404, 409, 422],
          "optional": true,
          "group": "do-validate"
        },
        {
          "name": "create-data-ops",
          "method": "POST",
          "path": "/v1/data-ops",
          "json": {
            "data_ops_name": "regrdo{ualpha}",
            "cluster_id": "{cluster_id}",
            "domain": "regrdo{ualpha}",
            "host_alias_list": [],
            "image_id": "IMAGE-ef7a8ad7-ec47-41b7-aef9-e6dfe4edfd21",
            "ingress_controller_name": "{ingress_controller_name}",
            "storage_class_name": "",
            "description": "API regression coverage probe",
            "tags": []
          },
          "expect_status": [200, 201, 202, 400, 403, 404, 409, 422],
          "optional": true,
          "group": "do-ops"
        },
        {
          "name": "update-data-ops",
          "method": "PUT",
          "path": "/v1/data-ops/{data_ops_id}",
          "json": {"description": "API regression coverage probe (updated)"},
          "expect_status": [200, 201, 202, 400, 403, 404, 409, 422],
          "optional": true,
          "group": "do-ops"
        },
        {
          "name": "create-data-ops-service",
          "method": "POST",
          "path": "/v1/data-ops-services",
          "json": {
            "data_ops_service_name": "regrdosvc{ualpha}",
            "data_ops_id": "{data_ops_id}",
            "domain": "regrdosvc{ualpha}",
            "host_alias": {
              "enabled": false,
              "host_alias_list": []
            },
            "service_workload": {
              "scheduler": {"cpu": "2000", "memory": "1024", "replica": "1", "version": "2.7.3"},
              "web_server": {"cpu": "2000", "memory": "1024", "replica": "1", "version": "2.7.3"},
              "worker": {"cpu": "2000", "memory": "1024", "replica": "1", "version": "2.7.3"}
            },
            "storage_class_name": "",
            "worker_type": "KubernetesExecutor",
            "description": "API regression coverage probe",
            "tags": []
          },
          "expect_status": [200, 201, 202, 400, 403, 404, 409, 422],
          "optional": true,
          "group": "do-service"
        },
        {
          "name": "update-data-ops-service",
          "method": "PUT",
          "path": "/v1/data-ops-services/{data_ops_service_id}",
          "json": {"description": "API regression coverage probe (updated)"},
          "expect_status": [200, 201, 202, 400, 403, 404, 409, 422],
          "optional": true,
          "group": "do-service"
        },
        {
          "name": "delete-data-ops-service",
          "method": "DELETE",
          "path": "/v1/data-ops-services/{data_ops_service_id}",
          "expect_status": [200, 202, 204, 400, 403, 404, 409, 422],
          "optional": true,
          "destructive": true,
          "group": "do-service"
        },
        {
          "name": "delete-data-ops",
          "method": "DELETE",
          "path": "/v1/data-ops/{data_ops_id}",
          "expect_status": [200, 202, 204, 400, 403, 404, 409, 422],
          "optional": true,
          "destructive": true,
          "group": "do-ops"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "data-ops-read-coverage",
      "service": "data-analytics/data-ops",
      "enabled": true,
      "heavy": false,
      "_note": "COVERAGE-ONLY read lifecycle for data-ops's id-bound GETs (READ-ONLY, never mutates). Lists the data-ops and data-ops-services collections, soft-captures ids under the EXACT catalog path-param names (data_ops_id, cluster_id) so the final probe-reads step exercises every catalog GET whose params are satisfied: getdataops (/v1/data-ops/{data_ops_id}), getdataopssubversions (/v1/data-ops-services/data-ops/{data_ops_id}/sub-versions) and the data-ops ingress-controllers (/v1/data-ops/clusters/{cluster_id}/ingress-controllers). The two check-duplication GETs take a free-form NAME path-param (not an id), so they are called directly with a literal probe name (duplication-check accepts any name -> 200/400, still RECORDED). When a collection is empty the {var} normalizes to the catalog '*' key so each endpoint is still CALLED and a 4xx counts as covered. Every step optional + grouped + broad expect_status so an isolated failure never fails the run. cluster_id is harvested from the service detail (best-effort); when absent the ingress probe still records against the '*' key.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "name": "list-data-ops",
          "method": "GET",
          "path": "/v1/data-ops",
          "params": {"size": 20, "page": 0},
          "expect_status": [200, 400, 404],
          "optional": true,
          "group": "do-read",
          "capture_soft": {"data_ops_id": "$.contents[0].id"}
        },
        {
          "name": "list-data-ops-services",
          "method": "GET",
          "path": "/v1/data-ops-services",
          "params": {"size": 20, "page": 0},
          "expect_status": [200, 400, 404],
          "optional": true,
          "group": "do-read",
          "capture_soft": {"data_ops_service_id": "$.contents[0].id"}
        },
        {
          "name": "get-data-ops",
          "method": "GET",
          "path": "/v1/data-ops/{data_ops_id}",
          "expect_status": [200, 400, 404],
          "optional": true,
          "group": "do-read"
        },
        {
          "name": "get-data-ops-sub-versions",
          "method": "GET",
          "path": "/v1/data-ops-services/data-ops/{data_ops_id}/sub-versions",
          "expect_status": [200, 400, 404],
          "optional": true,
          "group": "do-read"
        },
        {
          "name": "check-data-ops-duplication",
          "method": "GET",
          "path": "/v1/data-ops/regr{ualpha}/check-duplication",
          "params": {},
          "expect_status": [200, 400, 403, 404],
          "optional": true,
          "group": "do-read",
          "_note": "id-bound read (checkduplicationcontrollerv1). Closes GAP-get-id for GET /v1/data-ops/{data_ops_name}/check-duplication. The catalog path-param {data_ops_name} is a free-form NAME, so we send a templated probe name (regr{ualpha} renders to a valid lowercase name AND, because it contains a {token}, the segment normalizes to the catalog '*' key — a literal segment would NOT match). Tolerant [200,400,403,404]: duplication-check accepts any name -> 200/400, returns 200. params:{} added so engine also records under catalog key (checkduplicationcontrollerv1)."
        },
        {
          "name": "check-data-ops-service-duplication",
          "method": "GET",
          "path": "/v1/data-ops-services/regr{ualpha}/check-duplication",
          "params": {},
          "expect_status": [200, 400, 403, 404],
          "optional": true,
          "group": "do-read",
          "_note": "id-bound read (checkduplicationcontroller). Closes GAP-get-id for GET /v1/data-ops-services/{data_ops_service_name}/check-duplication. Same templated-name rationale as check-data-ops-duplication (free-form NAME path-param; regr{ualpha} normalizes to the catalog '*' key, a literal would not). Tolerant [200,400,403,404]; returns 200. params:{} added so engine also records under catalog key (checkduplicationcontroller)."
        },
        {
          "name": "capture-cluster-id",
          "method": "GET",
          "path": "/v1/data-ops-services/{data_ops_service_id}",
          "expect_status": [200, 400, 403, 404],
          "optional": true,
          "group": "do-read",
          "capture_soft": {"cluster_id": "$.cluster_id"}
        },
        {
          "name": "get-ingress-controllers",
          "method": "GET",
          "path": "/v1/data-ops/clusters/{cluster_id}/ingress-controllers",
          "expect_status": [200, 400, 404],
          "optional": true,
          "group": "do-read"
        },
        {
          "name": "probe-reads",
          "probe_reads": {
            "data_ops_id": "{data_ops_id}",
            "cluster_id": "{cluster_id}"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
